          "snippet": "Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive — Pedal Tone Profile How to Use It",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive — Songs That Use This Pedal and How to Dial It In | ToneMirror ToneMirror Tone matcher All tones Get started Browse the catalog Tones Artists Albums Genres Decades Amps Guitars Basses Pedals Brands Home › Pedals › Vox › Valvenergy Copperhead Drive Pedal · 2020–present Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive — Pedal Tone Profile How to Use It Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive — its tonal profile, specs, and how to recreate its sound on the gear you already own. No catalogued songs use this pedal yet, but ToneMirror can translate its voicing to your rig in under a minute. mid-forward high-gain gain premium tier Adapt to my gear Dial the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive sound in on your own rig Tonal profile Nutube-driven valve distortion voicing British full-stack rock — snappy Plexi crunch through JCM800 bite and on into modern hot-rodded Marshall gain. Gain and volume with a full treble/middle/bass stack, a bright switch and a mode switch, all-analog path with an OLED oscilloscope display. Pedal specs Type Pedal Brand Vox Production 2020–present Price tier Premium EQ voicing Mid-forward Gain structure High-gain Similar pedals Other Pedals in Our Catalog Pedal Vox V847 Wah 11 tone s Pedal Vox Tone Bender VBM1 1 tone Pedal Vox Big Bad Wah V847A-VBM 0 tone s Pedal Vox V845 Standard Wah 0 tone s Pedal Vox V848 Clyde McCoy Wah 0 tone s Pedal Vox V846-HW Hand-Wired Wah 0 tone s Your rig isn&#x27;t a Vox? Doesn&#x27;t matter. Get the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive Sound Translated for Your Gear ToneMirror translates the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive&#x27;s voicing — its EQ curve, gain structure, and response — onto whatever pedal you actually own, so you can chase its sound without owning one. Adapt to my gear FAQ Common Questions About the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive What does the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive sound like? Nutube-driven valve distortion voicing British full-stack rock — snappy Plexi crunch through JCM800 bite and on into modern hot-rodded Marshall gain. Gain and volume with a full treble/middle/bass stack, a bright switch and a mode switch, all-analog path with an OLED oscilloscope display. The signal-chain placement on each tone breakdown shows exactly where it sits relative to the rest of the rig. What are the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive&#x27;s key tonal traits? The Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive is characterized by mid-forward EQ, high-gain gain. ToneMirror uses exactly these traits when it translates a tone you pick onto your rig — or the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive&#x27;s sound onto whatever you own. When was the Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive made? The Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive has been in production since 2020. Do I need a Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive to play these songs? No — that&#x27;s the whole point of ToneMirror. The settings on every per-song page were originally dialed in on a Vox Valvenergy Copperhead Drive, but our match engine translates them to whatever pedal you actually own. Different drive characteristic, same recorded result. ToneMirror ToneMirror is for guitarists and bassists who&#x27;d rather spend their evening playing the song than chasing the tone. Browse Tones Artists Albums Genres Decades Amps Guitars Basses Pedals Brands Product Tone matcher How it works Tone library Built for your rig Pricing Get started Find your tone Sign in Contact support © 2026 ToneMirror. Made for players. Privacy Terms",
