          "snippet": "The Korg/Vox V829 Tone Bender - VOX Showroom",
          "bodyExcerpt": "The VOX Showroom - The Vox V829 Tone Bender ..... Help the VSR - Photos and Info Needed Contact the Vox Showroom UK VOX AMPS History of Vox in the UK JMI Era Vox Amps: 1959-65 JMI Era UL Series Hybrid Amps: 1966-67 JMI-VSL Era Solid State Amps: 1967-73 VSEL/Corinthian Era Vox Tube Amps: 1968-70 Birch Stolec Era Vox Amps: 1970-73 Dallas Era Vox Amps: 1973-78 Rose Morris Era Vox Amps: 1978-92 Korg Era Tube Amps 1993-25 Korg Era Solid State and Hybrid Vox Amps:1999-25 Korg Era Vox Valvetronix Amps - 2001-16 US VOX AMPS VOX ORGANS VOX GUITARS Vox Solid Body Elec Guitars: 1960-88 Vox Semi-Acoustic Elecric Gtrs: 1964-68 Vox Acoustic Guitars: 1964-70 Vox Bass Guitars: 1962-87 Voxton Guitars Basses: 1969-70 Vox Gtrs Basses, Korg Era: 1998-25 VOX FX MISC View All Products Vox Tape Echo Reverb Units:1963-68 Vox Microphones and Mixers Vox Boosters Vox Wah Wah Pedals: 1967-2025 Vox Effects Pedals: 1965-2025 Vox Tonelab Stomplab FX Processors Vox Amplugs Vox Ampliphonic Accessories: 1968 Vox Accessories Vox Promotional Items VOX SALES LITERATURE VOX MANUALS MY VOX BAND SEARCH WHAT'S NEW The Korg/Vox V829 Tone Bender 2_Footer &copy; 1996 - 2026 The Vox Showroom, all rights reserved. No use on online auctions, eBay or Reverb. The Vox V829 Tone Bender &quot;Fuzz&quot; was one of first products introduced under the Korg ownership of the Vox brand. It was included in the 1994, 1995, 1996 and 1997 Vox price lists and featured in a 1994 sales flyer . The V829 was based on the circuitry of the V828 Tone Bender that was produced during the Thomas Organ ownership period of Vox (1965 - 1971). The V828 Tone Bender was manufactured for Thomas Organ by the Italian manufacturer JEN. The JMI version of the Tone Bender was produced by Sola Sound of London. The circuitry for both the V828 and V829 Tone Benders utilized two PNP germanium transistors. Sola installed a pair of European OC76 V828 Tone Bender transistors into the UK model. JEN installed an SFT363 and an SFT337 transistor into the version of the V828 Tone Bender sold in the North American market place. The Thomas Organ V828 service manual indicated that if European specification transistors were not available, a pair of SK3004 germanium transistors would be a suitable field replacement. The Korg/Vox V829 Tone Bender used a pair of these SK3004 germanium transistors. 3_Footer Contents &bull; UK Vox Amplifiers &bull; US Vox Amplifiers &bull; Vox Organs &bull; Vox Guitars Vox Effects &bull; My 1960's Vox Band &bull; What's New &bull; Search the Vox Showroom US Vox Schematics &bull; UK Vox Schematics &bull; Vox Catalogs &bull; Owners Manuals Photos and editorial content courtesy Gary Hahlbeck Any and all material presented herein is protected by Copyright. &copy; 1998 - 2026 The Vox Showroom, all rights reserved The images and editorial content in this web site may not be copied or reproduced in online auction sites such as eBay, Reverb and Craig's List. Sellers may provide a link to the Vox Showroom web site if they wish to refer to this copyrighted material. URL: https://www.voxshowroom.com/uk/amp/v829.html",
