          "snippet": "WALRUS AUDIO 385 OVERDRIVE MKII MANUAL Pdf Download",
          "bodyExcerpt": "WALRUS AUDIO 385 OVERDRIVE MKII MANUAL Pdf Download | ManualsLib Sign In Upload Download Table of Contents Contents Add to my manuals Delete from my manuals Share URL of this page: HTML Link: WALRUS AUDIO 385 OVERDRIVE MKII MANUAL Pdf Download '> Pinterest Bookmark this page Add Manual will be automatically added to \"My Manuals\" Print this page &times; Bookmark added &times; Added to my manuals Manuals Brands Walrus Audio Manuals Music Pedal 385 Overdrive MKII Manual Walrus Audio 385 Overdrive MKII Manual Hide thumbs 1 2 3 page of 3 Go / 3 Contents Table of Contents Bookmarks Table of Contents Bypass A/B Volume a Gain a Volume B Gain B Treble Bass 385+ Switch Specs Quick Links Download this manual The 385 Overdrive MKII is inspired by the vintage Bell and Howell that guitarists have modified and used as guitar amps for its unique breakup and tone. The 385 captures the amp's charm by running internally at 18 volts* to help nail the same dynamic feel and response to pick attack the amp has. Dig in and discover all the nuances the MKII has to offer. And yes, the dynamics of the 385 sound great on bass too! *Only use a 9 volt DC, Center Negative, 100mA to power the pedal. The use of an isolated power supply is recommended for powering all Walrus Audio Pedals. Email help@walrusaudio.com to talk with a real live human about your Walrus gear! Bypass: Soft-touch, relay true bypass. Press the switch to engage/disengage the pedal. LED indicates whether the circuit is engaged or not. A/B: The A/B switch allows you to have two separate volume and gain settings. Use it like a preset to change the volume and/or gain for specific parts! Press to swap between using either A (White) or B (Red) Volume and Gain controls. LED indicates which controls are being used - White for A, Red for B. Volume A: Controls the overall volume in the A setting. Turn clockwise for more volume, and counter-clockwise for less volume. Gain A: Controls the overall gain in the A setting. Turn clockwise for more gain, counterclockwise for less gain. Daisy chain power supplies are not recommended. Got questions or need a repair? This product comes with a limited lifetime warranty. Click Here for more info. 385 Filmosound projector &#xAE; &#x2122; Previous Page Next Page 1 2 3 Table of Contents Need help? Do you have a question about the 385 Overdrive MKII and is the answer not in the manual? Ask a question Related Manuals for Walrus Audio 385 Overdrive MKII Music Pedal Walrus Audio MAKO MKII ACS1 Quick Start Manual Amp + cab simulator (11 pages) Music Pedal Walrus Audio MAKO MKII R1 Quick Start Manual High-fidelity stereo reverb (10 pages) Music Pedal Walrus Audio Mako Series Instruction Manual High-fidelity stereo delay (7 pages) Music Pedal Walrus Audio MAKO M1 Instruction Manual High-fidelity modulation machine (11 pages) Music Pedal Walrus Audio CANVAS CLOCK Manual (12 pages) Walrus Audio MAKO MKII ACS1 Amp/Cab Simulator User Manual (article) Music Pedal Walrus Audio CANVAS STEREO Instruction Manual Dual line isolator & d.i. (2 pages) Walrus Audio MAKO MKII R1 reverb pedal User Manual (article) Summary of Contents for Walrus Audio 385 Overdrive MKII Page 1 And yes, the dynamics of the 385 sound great on bass too! *Only use a 9 volt DC, Center Negative, 100mA to power the pedal. The use of an isolated power supply is recommended for powering all Walrus Audio Pedals. Daisy chain power supplies are not recommended. Page 2 Volume B: Controls the overall volume in the B setting. Turn clockwise for more volume, and counter-clockwise for less volume. Gain B: Controls the overall gain in the B setting. Turn clockwise for more gain, counterclockwise for less gain. Treble: The Treble knob allows you to boost or cut treble frequencies. Table of Contents Print Print page 1 Print document (3 pages) Rename the bookmark Cancel Delete bookmark? Cancel Delete Delete from my manuals? Cancel Delete manuals lib About Us F.A.Q. What Our Users Say Press & Medi