        {
          "url": "https://www.wamplerpedals.com/products/distortion-overdrive/wampler-black-65/",
          "host": "www.wamplerpedals.com",
          "title": "Black ’65 Limited Edition | Wampler Pedals",
          "h1": "Black ’65 Limited Edition",
          "description": "There was something almost magical about certain amplifiers from the 1960’s. Wampler’s Black ‘65 pedal captures the tonal nuances and rich harmonics associated with this classic era!",
          "snippet": "Black &#x27;65 Limited Edition - Wampler Pedals",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Black ’65 Limited Edition | Wampler Pedals Home Shop All Pedals Distortion / Overdrive Compression Fuzz Delay / Reverb Modulation Boost Utilities Discontinued Plugins Merchandise Dealers Community Blog Artists Podcast Videos Support About Downloads FAQs Warranty Registration Withdrawal Request Contact Us search account_circle My Account search Products search Black ’65 Limited Edition There was something almost magical about certain amplifiers from the 1960’s. Wampler’s Black ‘65 pedal captures the tonal nuances and rich harmonics associated with this classic era! Out of stock Watch video Overview Features Videos Technical Downloads Out of stock &#8220;While the world moves increasingly toward digital modeling, these analog circuits offer something uniquely compelling.&#8221; Right facing | Front | Left facing | Back | Top |' data-navmenu=\"off\" data-hashurl=\"off\" data-menuSlider=\"off\" data-continue-autoplay=\"off\" data-outside-nav=\"off\" data-autoplay=\"off\" > 4 5 There was something magical about certain amps from the 1960s, amps that have become to be known as the \"blackface\" or \"black panel\" style of amplifiers from a certain legendary American guitar and amplifier company. With such a rich legacy of tone to follow, Grand Pappy BDub’s take on the American-voiced amps of that period was turned into the legendary Black ‘65 Pedal. Through a clean amp, this pedal offers a faithful reproduction of the tones Brian loved from this classic period, and it is also flexible enough to add a new level of nuanced grit to your existing rig. This is a limited edition pedal and only available to purchase online here from Wamplerpedals.com. Once they’re gone, they’re gone! &#36; 199.97 Out of stock SKU: WMP-B65-PED Category: Distortion / Overdrive Tags: AIAB , Amp , Black 65 warning Cancer and Reproductive Harm www.p65warnings.ca.gov Limited Edition, Classic Tones Although the Black ’65 delivers the sound of those vintage tones you have come to love and expect, it is not limited to only one particular sound. With a 3 band eq similar to a vintage ”black panel” amp, you’re able to sculpt the tonality, feel, compression and overall gain structure just like you would on the real tube amplifier it’s emulating. Get Boosted The Boost switch controls the amount of internal gain available to the pedal – handy when dealing with different guitar output levels or just as some extra grunt to push this into primitive breakup – very similar to high levels of rectification that became the trademark tonal quality of a famous Californian boutique amp manufacturer. Vintage Playability This pedal sounds great with every type of pickup we’ve thrown at it. Whether you are slinging a single coil, looking for that classic Nashville twang, or driving a Humbucker into a 4×12, this pedal will take your tone back to an era that defined the history of music and beyond. Amp in a Pedal This is one of Wampler’s legendary circuits reborn in a limited edition pedal that works great with any amplifier or even direct into your favorite cabinet sim or IR loader. Hear it in action: Technical Details Limited Edition Built in the U.S.A. High-grade components selected for superior sound and response Controls: Volume, Gain, Bass, Middle and Treble, Boost Switch Boost Switch toggles between lower and higher gain mode. Battery connection and 9V power jack This pedal draws approximately 3mA at 9V and 9mA at 18V. 2.5″ x 4.5″ x 1.5″ in size (63.5mm x 114.3mm x 38.1mm) – height excludes knobs and switches Black panel magic There was something almost magical about the “black panel” amplifiers of the 1960’s&#8230; Out of stock 5 Year Limited Warranty Each Wampler product that bears the official “Wampler – Built in USA” logo is custom designed and assembled in the USA using premium globally sourced components chosen for superior sound and response. Each pedal comes complete with Wampler’s 5 year limited warranty – we stand by our products so you can stomp on them! Register Product Looking for O",
